# CODEOWNERS
#
# These were `@OctaCore-Technologies/*` — teams from a different org, carried in
# with the rest of the scaffold. That org exists, so nothing looked wrong, but
# its teams have no access to this repo and GitHub silently ignores an owner it
# can't resolve. `require_code_owner_review` is set on both rulesets and was
# matching nobody: PRs opened with zero reviewers auto-requested.
#
# Verified 2026-09-19 (UTC+8, so 2026-09-18 UTC): pm, qa, frontend and backend
# all exist under Haven-Care with write access. Re-check after any org or team
# rename — the failure mode is silent, and the symptom is a PR that requests no
# reviewers.
#
# These owners do not single out PM and QA, and that is deliberate. Code-owner
# review is satisfied by any ONE matching owner, so two @Haven-Care/frontend
# approvals clear both that rule and the 2-approval count on main. Any two
# reviews are fine — the count is the control, not who casts it.
#
# If that ever needs to change, the lever is the ruleset's `required_reviewers`
# (one entry per team, each with minimum_approvals), not this file. Listing
# fewer owners here would only narrow who *can* review, not require anyone.
#
#   gh api repos/Haven-Care/Bernardos-Maternity-and-Lying-in-Clinic/teams \
#     -q '.[] | "\(.slug) \(.permission)"'

# Global fallback — anything not matched by a rule below is owned by PM and QA
